ple being on so maybe parties will happen more   frequently now as wellThat's it for the wizzes/gods so that they/you won't change things ;)Drude**Hi all,Maybe I've missed something again but at the moment I really do not know whereor which guild has the spell word 'huh' so that I can identify monsters ...Isn't the sub-guild in the game at the moment??Cheers, Drude**  Hi,I'm wondering is there something going to be done with the questpoints?Right now i've got a couple of them and would like to use them while gainingmy levels as before. Since this isn't possible at the moment for some reasonhow else then are we supposed to use them since the help-files clearly statethat one should try and gain questpoints.That's all, DrudeNB. might it be a good idea to transform them into tps??**Thanks for the wizzes who made the second locker room work bug-free.Finally the change to store both a complete fighter and a complete mageand a complete defender set.We're happier again  :-)**As all of you people know, in this mud you need to train your skills asadjectives, not as percents as some muds have made it.It is widely known that each adjective has 5 steps.But as far as i can remember, there is no thing that would tell youwhich step you are working on.I am not saying this is compulsory to have or that we cannot live without it,but i think it would make our lives lot more easy.Thank you. I have spoken.-------- Proge --------**I don't know if i have done something wrong, but...I had eq's one day, and I put them into keep.Then i got around making exp and finding myself someequipments that i do appreciate very high.That's why i got into shop.So, I was in the shop and sold some equipments when I realized that I have sold and eq i was having [in keep].This didn't piss me off, but I thought that maybe people whohave more valuable items with them and want tokeep them with themselves would not like whentheir equipments which are not free, as i recall,are lost in the shop.So, if there is a bug with the 'keep', you could fix it.i think that it is one of the most needed commands in MUD.All the best,PROGE**"
